WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.810
"Every member of the Spellman family is born
with a twin!"

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:09.259
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm explaining all the chilling

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:13.259
clues that Sabrina may have a twin who hasn't
been revealed yet!

00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:17.039
Keep watching to the end to find out who it's
most likely to be!

00:00:17.039 --> 00:00:20.529
Spoilers ahead, so take care if you're not
all caught up, otherwise tap here to watch

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:22.660
my spoiler-free review.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:27.050
The origins of the twin theory begin right
in the very first episode of Chilling Adventures

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:31.130
in the scene where Sabrina is taking a bath
and suddenly has a vision which transports

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.590
her into the woods.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:36.780
She sees her parents holding a crying baby,
and as she follows them, she discovers two

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:37.780
babies.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:41.620
She lifts up the blanket covering them and
discovers one of the babies has cloven hooves

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.250
rather than human feet like the other child.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.800
The vision disappears, but it leaves us with
a lingering thought as to what it really means.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.140
On one level, this vision of two babies is
symbolic of Sabrina's dual nature – she's

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.540
half-witch and half-mortal.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:59.719
It also represents the decision that Sabrina
wrestles with throughout the first season.

00:00:59.719 --> 00:01:04.680
The cloven-hoofed baby on the left represents
her pledging allegiance to the Dark Lord and

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:09.680
the human baby on the right symbolizes the
mortal world Sabrina is trying to avoid leaving

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:10.680
behind.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:14.270
There's also some foreshadowing of Father
Blackwood's twins in this scene and I'll talk

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.590
more about that later.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:20.070
But in a show like Chilling Adventures, there
are often multiple layers of meaning to important

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:24.799
scenes like this one and fans of the old-school
Sabrina the Teenage Witch sitcom will remember

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:29.049
the line that "every member of the Spellman
family is born with a twin."

00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:33.700
Curiously, the Chilling Adventures of Sabrina
has already been exploring the idea of secret

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.420
twins in its first season.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:40.409
In the season 1 finale, Zelda steals away
Blackwood's first-born daughter to raise with

00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:44.509
Hilda, leaving the High Priest with what he
thinks is an only son, unaware that little

00:01:44.509 --> 00:01:47.440
Judas actually has a twin sister.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:51.880
In episode 5, "Dreams in a Witch House", the
Spellmans end up being tortured by the sleep

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:56.479
demon Batibat, and during Hilda's nightmare,
Principal Hawthorne reveals that, unknown

00:01:56.479 --> 00:02:00.630
to most people except his mother, he had a
twin brother who he absorbed while in the

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:01.630
womb.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:05.479
During that same nightmare, Hilda has a vision
that she and Zelda have been sewn together

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:08.140
and become inseparable like conjoined twins.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:13.270
Indeed, it's interesting that the show's production
designer Lisa Soper told website Black Girl

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:18.000
Nerds that she thinks of Hilda and Zelda as
conjoined twins; in fact, that's why she created

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.790
that single chair the sisters share in their
office.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:25.400
Obviously these last two examples in episode
5 are visions and demonstrate Hilda's fear

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:29.950
of a never-ending co-dependence with her sister,
but they also show that Chilling Adventures

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:35.100
is rather interested in the idea of twins
and the storytelling opportunities they afford.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.430
And Zelda taking away Lady Blackwood's daughter
to raise in secret, brings up an interesting

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.870
theory that Zelda and Hilda already did this
with another baby.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.260
"We can raise her.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.650
We've done it before."

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:48.580
"We'll keep it a secret, you and I.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:49.810
Together, as sisters."

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:54.120
Most of us probably assumed Zelda was referring
to how she and Hilda raised Sabrina after

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.650
her parents died, but what if she really means
the two aunties secretly raised the other

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.230
baby that Sabrina saw in her vision?

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:05.130
Fans of the old-school Sabrina show have seen
something like this before.

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:10.201
In the 90s sitcom, Sabrina meets her identical
twin Katrina at the end of the third season

00:03:10.201 --> 00:03:14.340
and it becomes a humorous plot point when
they have to undergo a test to find out which

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.010
sibling is the evil one.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:20.870
The test, of course, reveals Sabrina's sister
Katrina as the evil sibling, and Katrina is

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:24.780
then sent to live in the Twin Cities in a
place known as the "Other Realm".

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:29.760
In that show, the Other Realm is a separate
dimension accessed via a portal and Chilling

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.420
Adventures has already shown us a similar
[albeit darker] alternate dimension, Limbo.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:39.650
Access to Limbo is also through a portal and,
in the scenes we've seen so far, we've also

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.190
heard the sound of babies crying there.

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:46.790
We know from Sabrina's mother, Diana, that
unbaptized babies are sent to Limbo, so is

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:51.460
it possible that Sabrina's potential sibling
is stuck in Limbo similar to how Sabrina's

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.940
twin, Katrina, was stuck in the Other Realm
in The Teenage Witch show?

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:59.820
There's another possible twin clue in what
Sabrina's mother says to her in Limbo:

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.610
"But they took her."

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:04.510
"They took my baby after the baptism."

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.340
"Who did?

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:09.090
Are you okay?"

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:12.060
What Diana says to Sabrina could mean a couple
of things.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:16.730
It could suggest that Sabrina was taken away
from her mother after her Christian baptism

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.660
and then promised to the Dark Lord.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:22.650
Zelda witnessed the pledge Sabrina's father
made to the Dark Lord but she appeared to

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:27.480
be totally unaware of Sabrina's Christian
baptism, so unless Zelda is hiding something

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:31.230
about this, it could be that Diana is referring
to someone else.

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:35.660
Could it be that Diana had a second child,
perhaps a twin of Sabrina, and that baby was

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:36.910
taken away from her?

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:40.730
So, who are the likely candidates for Sabrina's
secret twin?

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:45.260
One possibility is Connor Kemper, the young
warlock who arrived at the Spellman Mortuary

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:46.940
in the first episode.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:50.570
His death is still a mystery at the end of
season 1 and I'm assuming it's something that

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:53.060
will be tackled in the second season.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:57.620
Someone who could be an especially interesting
reveal as Sabrina's twin is Nick Scratch.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:01.940
Nick seems to be a genuine friend of Sabrina's
and he supported her when she objected to

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.220
the Feast of Feasts.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:07.512
However, he could be hiding a darker side
which would play nicely into the idea of an

00:05:07.512 --> 00:05:08.870
evil twin.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:13.890
The clue to his darker nature may be hiding
in plain sight, and it's actually his name,

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:14.890
Nick Scratch.

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:19.940
"Old Nick" and "Old Scratch" are both nicknames
for the Devil, so could he be the dark twin,

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:23.010
or even the devil himself in disguise?

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:26.890
We know Nick is into Sabrina and with Sabrina
looking like she's going a bit wicked at the

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:30.930
end of the season, there's a hint she could
hook up with him in Season 2 [before they

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.550
realise they're related, if indeed they are].

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:38.780
So, we might be looking at a Luke and Leia
Skywalker or Jon Snow and Daenerys Targaryen

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:39.890
situation!

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:43.660
Other possibilities for Sabrina's twin could
be the Weird Sister Dorcas, who we've been

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:49.330
told is an orphan, or perhaps a new character
we'll meet in season 2, somebody who's stuck

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:52.510
in Limbo, or possibly even a character from
Riverdale?

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:56.880
Now, do you think Season 2 of Chilling Adventures
will reveal a twin for Sabrina?

